-- title:
--   Maximal ideals of the level-two ring are λ-nodes
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ a ring homomorphism. Let $a\in k$ satisfy $a^{q^2}=a$, $a\in\{0,1728\}$, and lie in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Let $K\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a number field, write $A_0=\mathrm{coeffSubring}\,A\,K=A\cap K$ with the restricted reduction $\mathrm{red}_0\colon A_0\to k$, and assume the kernel of $\mathrm{red}_0$ is the principal ideal generated by some $\varpi\in A_0$. Let $l\in k$ satisfy $a\,(16l)^2(16l-1)^2=256\bigl((16l)^2-16l+1\bigr)^3$ and admit a lift $y\in A_0$ with $\mathrm{red}_0(y)=l$. Let $R_0=\mathrm{modularLocalizedAtPoint}\,(1\cdot q)\,A_0\,\mathrm{red}_0\,a\,a^q$, the subring of Laurent series $f$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for which there are $r,s\in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ with $s(a,a^q)\ne 0$ (after reduction) and $f\cdot s(j,j_q)=r(j,j_q)$; assume $R_0$ is Noetherian and local. Let $B$ be a subring of Laurent series consisting exactly of those $z$ lying in $\mathrm{lambdaFieldOver}\,q\,K$ — the subfield generated by the constant series from $K$ together with $\lambda$ and $\lambda(q\,\cdot)$ — and integral over the image of $R_0$ under the substitution $\mathfrak q\mapsto\mathfrak q^2$ given by `qExpand … 2`. Then for every maximal ideal $Q$ of $B$ there exist $l'\in k$ with $a\,(16l')^2(16l'-1)^2=256\bigl((16l')^2-16l'+1\bigr)^3$, a lift $y'\in A_0$ with $\mathrm{red}_0(y')=l'$, an inclusion $B\le S_{l'}:=\mathrm{lambdaLocalizedAtPoint}\,q\,A_0\,\mathrm{red}_0\,l'\,l'^q$ (the series $f$ with $f\cdot s(\lambda,\lambda_q)=r(\lambda,\lambda_q)$ for some $r,s$ with $s(l',l'^q)\ne 0$), and a proof that $S_{l'}$ is local, such that $Q$ is the contraction of the maximal ideal of $S_{l'}$ along this inclusion.
--
--   This identifies the maximal ideals of the level-two ring $B$ over a supersingular node $(a,a^q)$ of $X_0(q)$ with $j$-invariant $0$ or $1728$: each of them is cut out by a $\lambda$-node $(l',l'^q)$ lying above $a$, in the sense of being the contraction of the maximal ideal of the corresponding localisation $S_{l'}$. It feeds the construction of the subring whose adic completion realises the equaliser of a stabiliser action at such points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_LambdaNodeLocalized_exists_eq_comap_maximalIdeal_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_of_isMaximal.lean

